Rules for variables 
1)A variable name must start with a letter, underscore (_), or dollar sign ($).
2)A variable name cannot start with a digit.
3)Variable names cannot contain spaces.
4)Java keywords cannot be used as variable names (e.g., int, class, public).
5)Variable names are case-sensitive (age and Age are different).
6)A variable name can contain letters, digits, underscores, and dollar signs.
7)Every variable must have a valid data type.
8)A variable must be declared before it is used.
9)Local variables must be initialized before they are used.
10)Variable names should be meaningful and descriptive.
